  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "An old bug which was fixed many releases ago has cropped up again. :(\n\nWhen booting up the latest release of VRChat in Steam using an Oculus headset (I have a Rift S in particular) the touch controller positions are tracked properly, but the buttons on the right controller do nothing while the buttons on the left controller press BOTH the left and right controller buttons simultaneously!\n\nFortunately, the workaround for this bug in the past also still works: If you take the battery out of your left touch controller specifically, boot VRChat, get into a game world, then put the battery back in, both controllers now work perfectly.",
